{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609ed45aa31cb1d9766990d31695403480cac39b14c0e2dbfd6af4687a711"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5x=10 \\\\ 4y=-12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $x$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. \n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x+0y=10 \\\\ 0x+4y=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609ed45aa31cb1d9766990d31695403480cac39b14c0e2dbfd6af4687a711"} {"question" "q-317506" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317506" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3