 | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-7$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-7$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y=10 \\\\ 5x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609ed45aa31cb1d9766990d31695403480cac39b14c0e2dbfd6af4687a711"} {"question" "q-317494" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "