" "value" "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y-2x=9 \\\\ -5y\\,=-15,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=9 \\\\ 0x-5y=-15\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "1cf2d7cff521a3af2b075976fb8fe8e0cb1fa5b3ecaca0d07086eea6a36a616a"} {"question" "q-317530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy 